        "original_id": "cdb1dabb-c257-5dfb-bf4e-b73416b3369f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lionel Hollins, Mike Fratello, Pete Maravich\n- Teams: Memphis Grizzlies, Brooklyn Nets, Philadelphia 76ers, Portland Trail Blazers, Boston Celtics\n- Roles: Head coaches, guard, TNT analyst\n- Seasons: 1979–80 Philadelphia 76ers season, 2004–05 Memphis Grizzlies season\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1979–80 Philadelphia 76ers season, the Philadelphia 76ers acquired guard Lionel Hollins from the Portland Trail Blazers after their attempt to obtain Pete Maravich failed because he signed with the Boston Celtics.\n- The 2004–05 NBA season was the Memphis Grizzlies' tenth season in the National Basketball Association and their fourth season in Memphis.\n- During the 2004–05 Memphis Grizzlies season, the Grizzlies lost four straight games under Lionel Hollins before replacing him with TNT analyst Mike Fratello.\n- Lionel Hollins most recently served as the head coach of the Brooklyn Nets in the National Basketball Association.",
